<title>MEXICO: Gamesa to invest $30 mln to update plants.</title>
<headline>Gamesa to invest $30 mln to update plants.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican cookie company Gamesa, a subsidiary of PepsiCo, plans to invest $70 million in 1997 to modernize its six plants in Mexico, the company said on Friday.</p>
<p>The company also plans to export to Costa Rica, Honduras and Guatemala for the first time, company director Salvador Alva told Reuters in an interview.</p>
<p>Gamesa's output fell five percent during 1996 because of high international wheat prices and the weak economy, but exports rose 10 percent.</p>
<p>Alva said he expects output to begin growing again this year.</p>
<p>((--Jacqueline Lerma, Redaccioon Monterrey, 528 345-7677))</p>
